CAT = "nzreAgency"; SEG = "AGY"
Q = [
("An agent has worked hard on a listing but never had a signed agency agreement. Is commission owed under the Act?",
 "No, a signed agreement is needed", ["Yes, if the vendor sold the home", "Yes, on a verbal promise alone", "Yes, if the buyer was introduced"],
 "Section 126 says an agent is not entitled to commission or expenses unless the work is done under a written agency agreement signed by or for the client and the agent."),
("The client signs an agency agreement today. By when must the agent give the client a copy signed for the agent?",
 "Within 48 hours of signing", ["Within 7 days of signing", "Within 10 working days", "Before the first open home"],
 "Section 126(1)(c) requires a copy signed by or for the agent to be given to the client within 48 hours after the client signed."),
("An agent forgot to give a copy within 48 hours, by honest oversight. Can a court still allow commission?",
 "Yes, if it is fair and just", ["No, the right is lost for good", "Yes, but only half is payable", "Yes, if the vendor later agrees"],
 "Section 126(2) and (3) let a court order commission recoverable despite late delivery if the failure was inadvertent or beyond the agent's control, the sum is fair and refusing would be unjust."),
("Before a vendor signs an agency agreement for residential property, what must the licensee provide?",
 "The approved guide and receipt", ["A copy of the LIM report", "A registered valuer's report", "A copy of the title search"],
 "Section 127 requires the approved guide on selling residential property to be given before signing, with the person's signed acknowledgement of receipt."),
("An agent skips the approved guide before signing a residential agency agreement. What is the effect on the agreement?",
 "It remains legally valid", ["It is void immediately", "It becomes a general agency", "It lapses after 90 days"],
 "Section 127(3) says contravening the guide requirement does not affect the validity of the agency agreement, though the agent is in breach."),
("A vendor is to repay marketing expenses. What must the agency agreement show about rebates or discounts on those expenses?",
 "Their source and estimated sum", ["Nothing, they belong to the agent", "Only that some rebates exist", "Only the final total they spent"],
 "Section 128 says no expenses are recoverable unless the agreement identifies the source of every rebate, discount or commission on them and estimates the amounts where reasonable."),
("What does a sole agency agreement mean for the client?",
 "No other agent may be used", ["The client may still use other agents", "The agent may sell without client consent", "The agent cannot be replaced"],
 "Section 4 defines a sole agency agreement as one where the client agrees not to instruct any other agent to act in respect of the transaction."),
("A vendor signs a sole agency agreement on Monday afternoon and receives their copy that day. By when can the vendor cancel it under section 130?",
 "5 pm on the next working day", ["Within seven calendar days", "Within 48 hours of signing", "By 5 pm on the third working day"],
 "Section 130 lets a client cancel a sole agency by written notice by 5 pm on the first working day after the copy was given, whatever the agreement says."),
("How may a client give notice of cancellation under section 130?",
 "By written notice or email", ["Only by registered post", "Only in person at the office", "Only through a solicitor"],
 "Section 130(2) says the cancellation notice may be served by fax or email."),
("An agent shows a buyer around, then the vendor cancels the sole agency within the cooling-off period. That buyer later contracts to buy. Can the agent still claim?",
 "Yes, if earlier effort led to it", ["No, cancellation ends any claim", "Yes, but only for expenses paid", "No, unless the buyer also pays"],
 "Section 130(4) lets an agent rely on the agreement despite cancellation if, before cancellation, the agent did agency work under it that enabled the contract."),
("A sole agency for a house is signed for a six-month term. When can a party cancel under section 131?",
 "After 90 days, by written notice", ["Only at the end of six months", "Only with the other side's consent", "Only if the agent breaches it"],
 "Section 131 lets any party to a residential sole agency longer than 90 days cancel by written notice at any time after the first 90 days, whatever the agreement says."),
("An agency agreement turns a sole agency into a general agency after 90 days, so the vendor must cancel to leave. This kind of clause is called:",
 "A roll-over clause", ["A cooling-off clause", "A conjunction clause", "A holdover clause"],
 "A roll-over clause, which REA material says may be an unfair term and may breach rule 9.12 and section 131 in a residential agreement, converts a sole agency into a general one."),
("What is a general agency?",
 "A non-exclusive agency", ["An agreement covering several properties", "An agency limited to commercial land", "An agency that acts for the buyer"],
 "A general agency is not exclusive: the client can also use other agencies or sell privately, with a separate agreement for each agency."),
("A vendor has signed with Agency A and wants to also sign with Agency B. What must the licensee explain under rule 9.10?",
 "Full commission to more than one", ["Commission is always split equally", "The second agreement is void", "Only the first agency gets paid"],
 "Rule 9.10 requires the licensee to explain that if other agency agreements exist, the client could be liable to pay full commission to more than one agent if a transaction concludes."),
("An agency agreement is cancelled. Under rule 9.11, what must the agent tell the client in writing?",
 "Names of customers it would claim", ["The customer list for open homes", "The licensee's own commission share", "The vendor's lowest accepted price"],
 "Rule 9.11 says on notice of cancellation the agent must advise the client in writing of each customer for whom the agent would claim commission if that customer concluded a transaction."),
("A clause says the vendor must pay a large fee if they simply change their mind about selling. Which rule is most relevant?",
 "Conditions must be necessary", ["Conditions must be agreed by a lawyer", "Fees must be fixed in dollars", "Terms are set by the Authority"],
 "Rule 9.12 says an agent must not impose conditions through an agency agreement that are not reasonably necessary to protect the agent's interests."),
("A licensee hands a vendor an agency agreement to sign with the fee section left blank, to be filled in later. This breaches:",
 "The rule on material particulars", ["The rule on recommending legal advice", "The rule on record keeping", "The rule on advertised prices"],
 "Rule 9.9 prohibits submitting an agency agreement or other contractual document for signature unless all material particulars are inserted or attached."),
("Before a prospective client signs an agency agreement, the licensee must recommend that they:",
 "Take legal advice", ["Obtain a registered valuation", "Seek a building report", "Get a LIM report first"],
 "Rule 9.7 requires a licensee to recommend legal advice, make sure the person knows they may need technical advice, and allow a reasonable opportunity to get it."),
("Before a seller signs, what must the licensee explain under rule 10.5?",
 "How choices affect their benefits", ["Why the market is still rising", "How the agency's fees are banked", "Why a sole agency is cheaper"],
 "Rule 10.5 requires the licensee to explain how choices the client may make about how to sell could affect the individual benefits the licensee may receive."),
("A seller's agency agreement sets out commission. Under rule 10.6, the written explanation must include:",
 "An estimated dollar commission", ["A promise of a minimum price", "The agency's trust account number", "The salesperson's own commission split"],
 "Rule 10.6(a) requires the conditions for paying commission and how it is calculated, including an estimated actual dollar cost based on the appraisal."),
("Rule 10.6 says the licensee must tell the client that they are not obliged to agree to:",
 "Additional marketing expenses", ["Any commission whatsoever", "A written agency agreement", "A listing price recommendation"],
 "Rule 10.6(c) and (d) require the written explanation to cover how the property will be marketed and any extra expenses, and that the client need not agree to those additional expenses."),
("For a buyer's agency agreement, the estimated commission under rule 11.2 is worked out using:",
 "Average of the estimated price range", ["The vendor's asking price", "The average sale price in the suburb", "The council's rating valuation"],
 "Rule 11.2(a) requires an estimated dollar commission based on the average of the estimated price range of the land the client is seeking to buy."),
("A licensee is authorised by the client to spend on advertising. What does rule 9.13 add?",
 "Seek the best value for them", ["Use the agent's preferred supplier", "Spend the whole budget set", "Get three quotes in every case"],
 "Rule 9.13 says when authorised to incur expenses, a licensee must seek to obtain the best value for the client."),
("A salesperson puts up a sale sign before the agency agreement has been signed. This:",
 "Breaches the marketing rule", ["Is fine if the vendor agreed verbally", "Is fine if no price is shown", "Is fine for a short while only"],
 "Rule 9.6 says unless authorised by a client through an agency agreement, a licensee must not offer or market land, including on a website or by a sign."),
("A salesperson receives a written offer. Under rule 10.10, to whom must it be submitted?",
 "The client, in full", ["Only the highest offer", "The agent's manager first", "Only the offers the vendor requested"],
 "Rule 10.10 requires a licensee to submit to the client all written offers for the land. Rule 10.11 requires an employed licensee to give the agent a copy of each."),
("How long must an agent keep a copy of each written offer submitted?",
 "12 months, sale or not", ["Three months after settlement", "Until settlement is complete", "For six months only"],
 "Rule 10.12 requires an agent to retain a copy of every written offer for 12 months, whether or not the offer resulted in a transaction."),
("Under REA's standard agency clauses, a vendor who ends a general agency must give how much written notice?",
 "Seven days", ["Forty-eight hours", "Fourteen days", "Thirty days"],
 "REA's agency agreement material says the standard clauses require seven days' written notice to cancel a general agency agreement."),
("Before a seller signs an agency agreement, which of these must the licensee set out in writing under rule 10.6?",
 "When the agreement ends", ["The vendor's likely sale price", "How many open homes are held", "Which lawyer will act for the buyer"],
 "Rule 10.6(b) requires the licensee to explain and set out in writing, among other things, when the agency agreement ends."),
]
